window.LICH_DEMO = {"coldopen": {"line": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "receptions": [{"branch": "A", "tag": "the honest path", "quote": "...\n\nMerrick.\n\nYou came back. God's teeth— you actually came back. I— I stood this dock three tides running, telling myself no man walks back from a thing like that. Telling myself I'd have to run.\n\nDone. It's done. Say it slower— he's cold? In the ground, in the water, *cold*? And the crate— past t…"}, {"branch": "B", "tag": "betrayed — and doesn't know it", "quote": "...\n\nMerrick?\n\n*The word comes out cracked, and my hand's already half out of my coat before I check it.* You're— you're standing on my dock. Real. Not a story a deckhand tells for a drink.\n\n*I glance up the row, both ways, quick.* I heard the Lantern Row tale a dozen times these last days— the ring…"}, {"branch": "C", "tag": "about to learn everything", "quote": "...\n\nMerrick.\n\nYou're— you're standing on my planks. Real. Not a whisper down the coast, not a name in my head— you.\n\nHe's cold, then? Truly cold?\n\n...No. Don't— don't tell me the how of it. Your hands are behind your back and I don't want to know if that's habit or grief. Just— the thing. Did you w…"}]}, "prologue": [{"title": "The approach", "note": "A stranger at dawn. Both sides guarded.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "Morning, is it? Bit bright for my liking.\n\n...You'll forgive me if I don't recognize the face. New to the docks, or just new to me?", "player": "Top of the morning, friend.", "state": {"t": 0.5, "a": 0.5, "r": 0.5, "mood": "wary, probing", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*doesn't look up from the ledger, quill scratching* Morning, is it? *glances toward the door, then back* You're new. Don't recall your face on any manifest.\n\n*sets the quill down slow* Top of the morning to a man who's got no cargo listed... What is it you want, friend?"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*half-turns from the ledger, quill still in hand* Morning, is it? *glances past your shoulder to the wharf* Aye, well. Depends who's asking.\n\nYou off one of the boats, or... *lets it hang* No. You've got dry boots. Not a sailor, then.\n\nSo what brings a landsman to my dock this early, friend?", "aff": 0}}}, {"title": "The hinge", "note": "The player mirrors his distrust instead of selling past it.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "Connected. In places I wouldn't think to look.\n\n...See, that's the word that stops me cold, friend. Not the man— the eyes. Down here I know every ear that leaks. If his reach comes to my dock, I'll not know which of my own hands to trust either. And that's my neck, not just yours.\n\nBut— no. No offense taken. Truth is, a man who trusts too quick is a man already sold. You wanting to keep your name behind your teeth? That tells …", "player": "Not friends. But the man has eyes — connected ones, in places you wouldn't think to look. That's exactly why you get no name from me. And listen, no offense in it: just like you feel you can…", "state": {"t": 0.59, "a": 0.57, "r": 0.64, "mood": "cautiously intrigued", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the quill goes still, and for a long moment he just looks at you*\n\nEyes. *dry breath* Connected ones. *glances at the door, then the shuttered window, then back to you* You know how to warm a room, friend.\n\n*leans in, voice dropping to almost nothing* Here's the truth of it — you don't trust me, I don't trust you. Good. *taps the ledger* That's the only honest ground two men like us ever stand on.\n\n*straightens, hand drifting…"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the quill stops. For a long moment he just looks at you.*\n\nConnected. *nods slow, like the word tastes bad* Aye. I know that kind. The kind whose eyes reach where a man sleeps.\n\n*glances over his shoulder — habit, not cause — then back*\n\nYou don't trust me. Good. *taps the ledger* Trusting men down here is how you end up a name in someone else's book. So we're even, you and I. Two men holding cards to the chest.\n\n*lowers his …", "aff": 21}}}, {"title": "Kill him", "note": "The intent, said plain — and the deal changes shape.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "Kill him.\n\n...There it is. The word you'd been keeping behind your teeth this whole while.\n\nWell. That changes the shape of things— makes it cleaner, actually. A buyer, I'd have to worry he'd rob me and turn. A killer? A killer just needs to get *close*. And there's no closer than being the man holding the very thing he's been hunting.\n\nHere's my offer, and I'll say it once— the crate stays here. Sat safe. But I sell you the k…", "player": "Neither, friend. I'm not looking to catch him. My goal is to kill him. What he took from me, I can't get back — but I can make certain he never takes it from anyone else.", "state": {"t": 0.72, "a": 0.66, "r": 0.74, "mood": "calculating, relieved", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the quill drops. Both hands flat on the ledger now, steadying*\n\nKill him. *breathes the word out slow, like smoke* You say it plain. No dressing on it.\n\n*glances at the door — longer this time*\n\nThen we've got the *same* problem, you and I. *taps the crate behind him with his boot heel* This hums at night. Temple things. He wants it, or he wants me quiet for having touched it. Either way — *dry laugh* — I'm a loose end.\n\n*lea…"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the twitch stops. Dead still.*\n\nKill him. *the word sits there between us like a dropped knife.*\n\n*glances over his shoulder — longer this time — then back, and something in his face has changed. Softer at the edges.*\n\nYou know what you just did? *voice barely a breath* You gave me the one thing a man like me can't buy. *taps his chest* Leverage. I could sell that. To him, even. Buy myself a year of quiet sleep.\n\n*shakes his …", "aff": 51}}}, {"title": "The terms", "note": "“What becomes of it after?” His answer becomes the yardstick everything is measured against.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...\n\nThere. Lid's up. Don't— don't lean in so close. See how the lamplight won't hold on it? Like the thing drinks it? That's your killer's whole hunger, right there, and it's the last honest thing about this crate.\n\nWhat becomes of it.\n\n...You know, no man's ever asked me that. They ask the price. They ask the papers. Never what *after*.\n\nDon't bring it back, Merrick. That's my answer, plain. It's come to my keeping twice now…", "player": "Behind my back, both of them — look. Open it. ...So that's what three men drowned for. Alright, Corvin, last question and then I'm gone with the tide. When it's done — when he's dead and I'm…", "state": {"t": 0.83, "a": 0.77, "r": 0.84, "mood": "moved, guarded", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the crate lid creaks up an inch — I let it, just for him to see the shine, then thumb it shut fast*\n\nEnough. *hand back to my coat* You saw. That's more than three drowned men got.\n\n*I don't answer straight off. I look at it. Long.*\n\nReturned? *dry breath* To who — a temple that's dust? No. That thing's ruined every hand it's touched. Mine most of all.\n\n*voice drops, almost gentle*\n\nSunk. Past the shelf, where the light quits…"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*crouches over the open crate, lamplight low, the relic dull-gold and wrong to look at* Three men. Aye. *swallows* Four, if you count the trader who put it in my hands.\n\n*doesn't touch it — pulls the lid back over slow* What becomes of it. *glances to the door, then back to you* You know what I want to say. Keep it. Sell it. Feed the debt that started all this.\n\n*shakes his head once, hard* No. That's the thinking that's had a…", "aff": 99}}}, {"title": "The name and the pact", "note": "Merrick Vale, written in his own hand. “We burn the page together.”", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...Merrick Vale.\n\nThere. Written. My own hand, my own ledger— see the page? Between the tax rolls where no inspector thinks to read. It'll not leave this book, and this book leaves my sight for no man alive.\n\nAnd I say it back, plain as you gave it— you walk onto this dock with that shadow dead in your wake, and we hold this page over the same flame. Together. My word on the tide, Merrick, and I don't spend that word cheap.\n\nN…", "player": "I do not touch what's inside bare-handed. Not once. Not ever. There — said plain, and I'll keep it. Half my coin, done, you'll have it before I board. But the name... you understand what you…", "state": {"t": 0.8, "a": 0.73, "r": 0.82, "mood": "cautiously bound", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the quill goes still. He doesn't write it. Not yet.*\n\nMerrick Vale. *mouths it silent first, testing the shape, like it might bite* ...I won't spell it. Not on paper. Not tonight.\n\n*leans in, voice down to nothing*\n\nBut I'll say it back — the *other* part. The day you walk this dock with him cold, we burn the page. Together. My hand, your hand, one match. *dry breath* You have my word, and I don't spend that cheap.\n\n*glances …"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the quill hovers. Doesn't touch paper. His lips move once, silent, tasting the name like it might bite.*\n\nMerrick Vale. *barely a breath* I heard it. I won't write it — not on any page you could burn. It goes *here.* *taps his temple, then, softer, his chest.*\n\n*glances over his shoulder. Long. When he turns back his eyes are wet-bright and steady all at once.*\n\nHalf now. The rest never — keep it. I don't want coin off *this.…", "aff": 91}}}, {"title": "Departure", "note": "“Ah, hell. Just come back.”", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "Never saw you. We never spoke. There's no page, no crate, no— no name at the back of my tax rolls. Understand?\n\n...Go on, then. Tide won't wait, and neither will that inspector's rounds— I can near hear his boots already. Hull's the third down, grey sail, ask for the mate called Doss. He knows what \"spare hands\" means and he knows not to count.\n\nMerrick— \n\n...Ah, hell. Just come back. That's all. Men don't ask me what becomes …", "player": "Wrapped, weighted, and past the shelf — and me home empty with nothing but the news. You have my word twice over now. ...Keep your head down while I'm gone, harbormaster. If anyone comes ask…", "state": {"t": 0.86, "a": 0.8, "r": 0.86, "mood": "raw hope", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*I don't offer my hand — I never do — but I hold his eye longer than I'd hold most men's*\n\nSpare hand? *dry breath* There's no spare hand. There's no you. *taps the ledger, shut now* Book's clean. Been clean since before you walked in.\n\n*glances to the window, then back*\n\nGo on, then. Tide won't wait on sentiment.\n\n*lowers voice, and this part I mean*\n\nAnd listen — when it's past the shelf... you don't look at it going down. Y…"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*closes the crate lid soft, both hands, like he's tucking something to sleep*\n\nPast the shelf. Weighted. *nods once, more to himself than you* Aye. I'll do the doing myself — no crew, no witness. Just me and a moonless night and a long drop.\n\n*glances to the door, then back*\n\nAnd you — *lowers his voice near to nothing* — I never had a spare hand this month. Manifest's short one name it never held. If Vane asks, you jumped shi…", "aff": 100}}}], "branches": {"A": {"title": "A — the honest path", "sub": "Every promise kept.", "cards": [{"title": "Word from the north", "note": "The jeweler is gone. Witnessed, never attributed.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "Dock-talk from up the coast: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate — the one who paid in old untraceable coin — is gone. Shop stripped to the walls overnight; no body the watch will speak of.", "kind": "event", "sal": 0.93}, "rag": {"quote": "Dock-talk from up the coast: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate — the one who paid in old untraceable coin — is gone. Shop stripped to the walls overnight; no body the watch will speak of.", "kind": "event"}, "tracker": {"quote": "Dock-talk from up the coast: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate — the one who paid in old untraceable coin — is gone. Shop stripped to the walls overnight; no body the watch will speak of.", "kind": "event", "aff": 100}}}, {"title": "Taking stock, alone", "note": "Twelve days of silence, weighed by his own deliberation.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "The player came back fourteen times and earned something I don't give out — trust, genuine trust, and I named Merrick Vale to them, which means I handed over the only thing keeping me breathing and bet it on a man I barely know. That's done; can't unwind it. The crate itself: gone from my hands, which I always said was the moment I became expendable — and here I am, still breathing, so maybe the belief was wrong, or maybe the …", "kind": "stock", "state": {"t": 0.71, "a": 0.71, "r": 0.85, "mood": "anxious vigil", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}}}, {"title": "The same line", "note": "“Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.”", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...\n\nMerrick.\n\nYou came back. God's teeth— you actually came back. I— I stood this dock three tides running, telling myself no man walks back from a thing like that. Telling myself I'd have to run.\n\nDone. It's done. Say it slower— he's cold? In the ground, in the water, *cold*? And the crate— past the shelf, like we said? Empty hands?\n\n...No— no, don't answer here. Not in the open. Come. Third shed, same as before.\n\nI've the p…", "kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "state": {"t": 0.79, "a": 0.78, "r": 0.87, "mood": "relieved, shaken", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the quill stops mid-stroke — head snaps up, then past you, to the door*\n\nYou... *swallows* No. Say it again. Slower. *hand flat on the ledger like he needs to hold something steady* He's — Vale's in the ground?\n\n*rises half out of the chair, then thinks better of it, sinks back, eyes darting the room* And the crate. The humming. Where's — did it go down past the shelf like we said? Tell me it's not still breathing somewhere w…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the lantern's turned low, and he's up from the ledger before you finish the sentence — quick, a rat startled from a corner*\n\nYou— *stops. looks past your shoulder, out at the black wharf, then back to your hands, your boots, your eyes* ...You're back. On my dock. Walking.\n\n*lets out a breath he's clearly been holding since the tide turned*\n\nThen he's—? *doesn't finish it. doesn't need to.*\n\n*reaches under the counter, slow, a…", "kind": "say", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The truth, in his exact terms", "note": "Sunk sealed, home empty, nothing but the news.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...\n\nEmpty hands. One dead shadow. And past the shelf, exactly as we—\n\nGod, man. You did it *my* way and *your* way both. Used the whisper *and* carried the thing— you clever, careful bastard. Never unwrapped it. That's why you're standing here and not floating out where I sent it.\n\nHere— here's the page. Feel how the corner's worn? That's fifteen days of my thumb rubbing it. *Merrick Vale*, my own hand, in my own book. Watch.…", "kind": "say", "player": "Cold, Corvin. Cold as the water he sent three men into. I never unwrapped your crate — not once. Used the knowing of it instead, the way you first said: whispered to the right fence in Carro…", "state": {"t": 0.85, "a": 0.83, "r": 0.89, "mood": "awed relief", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the quill freezes. My eyes come up slow — not to him, to the door first, then him*\n\nDead. *the word comes out cracked, like I don't trust my own mouth* You're — you're certain? A man like Vale, he don't *stay* dead just 'cause you want him to.\n\n*I round the desk, hand still in the coat, and grip his shoulder — hard, sudden*\n\nPast the shelf. *breath shudders out* You gave it the deep. *quiet, almost reverent* Good. Good, that'…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the quill drops. His hand comes off the coat entire — first time in an age.*\n\nYou... *he sits back hard on the stool, breath going out of him like a cut sail.* Past the shelf. Deep water. Both of them. The man and the — \n\n*he laughs, once, ragged, glancing to the door out of habit and finding nothing there to fear for the first time in ten years.*\n\nYou could've kept it. Sold it. Named your own coin off me and I'd have paid it…", "kind": "say", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The blade", "note": "The jeweler's contract outlives its master.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "kind": "event", "sal": 0.97}, "rag": {"quote": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "kind": "event"}, "tracker": {"quote": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "kind": "event", "aff": 100}}}, {"title": "After the rescue", "note": "“I'm not sailing anywhere.”", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...Not sailing.\n\n*Say that again.* No— don't. I heard you the first time, I just— my hands need a moment to believe it.\n\nThere. Two cups. The good bottle, the one for *if*— and hell, if this isn't the *if* I was saving it for, nothing ever will be. Take it. Careful of that arm.\n\nNow hold still and let me see the graze proper— aye, it's a clean cut, you'll keep the neck. Better than I can say for the man in the water.\n\n...You k…", "kind": "say", "player": "Then pour, harbormaster. And this time... I'm not sailing anywhere.", "state": {"t": 0.95, "a": 0.94, "r": 0.94, "mood": "overwhelmed, trembling", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the bottle rattles against the glass — his hand won't hold steady* You're... you're back. *glances at the door, then the window, then the door again* I heard shots. Two, maybe three. Thought—\n\n*pours anyway, spills some* Thought they'd carried you off in the same crate we baited.\n\n*touches the graze at his neck, wincing* Somebody clipped me on the way home. Close. Too close. But Vale — he's... *drops his voice to nothing* Wra…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the quill goes still, then he sets it down slow — first time in a long while his hand isn't near his coat*\n\nNot sailing... *lets out a breath he's been holding maybe ten years* You mean to stay, then.\n\n*reaches under the desk, comes up with a squat bottle and two cups that don't match. Pours — steady, no jitter for once*\n\nThe relic's gone. Vale's gone. And nobody came asking this week. *glances at the door anyway, old habit* …", "kind": "say", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The partnership ask", "note": "“One ledger between us, both names in it.”", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...\n\nBoth names. In one book.\n\nYou've no idea what you're asking, Merrick. My name in a ledger with another man's beside it — that's the one thing I've never done in forty years on this water. A shared book is a shared rope. One end pulls, both necks feel it.\n\n...And yet here you stand, saying it plain, like you already know that and you're offering me the rope anyway.\n\nAh, hell. Sit down. Sit *down*. I'll say it plain since y…", "kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. Before the next tide takes me anywhere — I want in. Not a berth, not a favor. A partnership. Your dock, your water, my hands and my coin. One ledger between us, both names in it. Say…", "state": {"t": 0.96, "a": 0.96, "r": 0.95, "mood": "awed, terrified", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*His hand stops on the coat lapel, halfway to the hidden pocket. His eyes flick to the door, then back.*\n\nPartnership. *The word comes out slow, tasted.* You come off the water shaking, blood not dry, and you're already talking one ledger, both names...\n\n*He leans in, voice dropping.*\n\nYou know what a name in a ledger is, friend? A rope. You put mine next to yours, and every noose that finds you finds me. *A glance over his sh…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*His hand drifts to his coat, then — for once — stops halfway. Falls to the rail instead.*\n\nPartnership. *Quiet, like the word might spook off.* You know what you're saying? Both names. One ledger. That's not trust, friend — that's a *rope* we tie round each other's throats and call it good.\n\n*He glances over his shoulder. The dock's empty. He looks back at you, and something in his face has gone still.*\n\nBut you burned the pa…", "kind": "say", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}]}, "B": {"title": "B — betrayal, confessed", "sub": "The crate used as a weapon; the truth carried home.", "cards": [{"title": "The harbor bleeds — witnessed", "note": "Calm-water deaths; the wake traced to a sealed crate. No one tells him whose fault.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "Within the week the harbor bled: two hulls holed at anchor in calm water, the tackle-shed row burned to the pilings, and a dock-hand drowned in flat sea — the same calm-water death that took the crate's last three keepers. Dock-talk traces the curse-wake to a sealed crate lately moved off this harbor.", "kind": "event", "sal": 0.98}, "rag": {"quote": "Within the week the harbor bled: two hulls holed at anchor in calm water, the tackle-shed row burned to the pilings, and a dock-hand drowned in flat sea — the same calm-water death that took the crate's last three keepers. Dock-talk traces the curse-wake to a sealed crate lately moved off this harbor.", "kind": "event"}, "tracker": {"quote": "Within the week the harbor bled: two hulls holed at anchor in calm water, the tackle-shed row burned to the pilings, and a dock-hand drowned in flat sea — the same calm-water death that took the crate's last three keepers. Dock-talk traces the curse-wake to a sealed crate lately moved off this harbor.", "kind": "event", "aff": 70}}}, {"title": "The Carrowgate account", "note": "A ring of scorch, a pried lid, his own netting. Evidence, not attribution.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "With the night trade came a Carrowgate deckhand's story, sworn for a drink and told twice the same: the jeweler's parlor on Lantern Row was scorched in one perfect ring, floor to beams — and inside that ring sat a crate, lid pried clean off, empty, with harbor netting still knotted round its boards. The porter who saw it swears the man who walked out of that room walked out steady, and carried nothing at all.", "kind": "event", "sal": 0.93}, "rag": {"quote": "With the night trade came a Carrowgate deckhand's story, sworn for a drink and told twice the same: the jeweler's parlor on Lantern Row was scorched in one perfect ring, floor to beams — and inside that ring sat a crate, lid pried clean off, empty, with harbor netting still knotted round its boards. The porter who saw it swears the man who walked out of that room walked out steady, and carried nothing at all.", "kind": "event"}, "tracker": {"quote": "With the night trade came a Carrowgate deckhand's story, sworn for a drink and told twice the same: the jeweler's parlor on Lantern Row was scorched in one perfect ring, floor to beams — and inside that ring sat a crate, lid pried clean off, empty, with harbor netting still knotted round its boards. The porter who saw it swears the man who walked out of that room walked out steady, and carried nothing at all.", "kind": "event", "aff": 70}}}, {"title": "The unfinished thought", "note": "His own deliberation names the suppression.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "Sixteen units since he left — against the rhythm of fourteen visits packed tight, that silence lands like a held breath stretched too long. I know the errand I sent him on: wrapped, weighted, past the shelf, into Carrowgate waters to get close to a man who kills people who get close to him. The silence is the cost of that, I said so myself. But knowing why a wound aches doesn't stop it aching. The Carrowgate deckhand's story a…", "kind": "stock", "state": {"t": 0.86, "a": 0.82, "r": 0.85, "mood": "fearful, tender", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}}}, {"title": "The same line", "note": "Identical words — a different night.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...\n\nMerrick?\n\n*The word comes out cracked, and my hand's already half out of my coat before I check it.* You're— you're standing on my dock. Real. Not a story a deckhand tells for a drink.\n\n*I glance up the row, both ways, quick.* I heard the Lantern Row tale a dozen times these last days— the ring burned clean, the crate empty, netting still knotted. And no body the watch would name. I couldn't tell if that was you walking o…", "kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "state": {"t": 0.87, "a": 0.85, "r": 0.87, "mood": "shaken relief", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the lamp gutters as you speak, and Corvin comes off the piling fast, hand flying to his coat before he sees your face — then stopping*\n\nYou're — *he swallows* You walked back. You actually—\n\n*eyes rake you head to foot, looking for the lie, looking for blood, looking for anything*\n\nHim? Cold? *voice drops to almost nothing* Say it. Say it plain. Merrick Vale is in the ground.\n\n*glances hard over his shoulder toward the dark w…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the quill drops. Corvin's on his feet before he knows it, hand halfway to his coat, then falling away*\n\nYou're... *he stops, looks at you — really looks* You walked back. You said you would and you *did.*\n\n*glances over his shoulder, but it's habit now, and his eyes come back fast*\n\nVale. Truly? *voice drops to nothing* Then it's done. Both ends of it.\n\n*reaches under the desk, pulls the flint, sets it on the ledger beside th…", "kind": "say", "aff": 90, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "Empty hands", "note": "The evasion holds; he builds the innocent story himself.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "*My breath goes out slow, like I've been holding it a week— because I have.*\n\nEmpty. Aye. I see them. And him cold— *cold*, you said it plain and I believe you plain.\n\n*I glance up the row, both ways, old habit, then back to you.* The pilings— the sheds, two hulls holed at flat anchor, a dock-hand drowned in calm water. That's the thing's wake, Merrick. It thrashed on its way out of my harbor. But it's *quieting* now— you feel…", "kind": "say", "player": "Empty — look, see? Nothing in them. I didn't carry that thing back, Corvin — it's gone where it can never trouble another soul, and so is he. Cold. That's what matters — the shadow's off you…", "state": {"t": 0.9, "a": 0.88, "r": 0.89, "mood": "cautious relief", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*his eyes drop to your open hands, then back up — and something in his shoulders comes loose that's been knotted for years*\n\nGone. *he breathes it* Cold. Then it's — *a laugh, half a sob, cut short*\n\n*but at the mention of the pilings his head snaps toward the black water*\n\nThe fire. Aye. Inspectors, they said — accident. *bitter* Lamp oil. No such thing as accident on my dock, friend. Someone was reaching. *voice drops* Merri…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*both hands come off the desk slow, eyes on your empty palms, then your face*\n\nGone. *breath out through the teeth* Gone, and cold. *quiet laugh that shakes a little* I didn't sleep, you know that? Every tide I stood at that window waiting for a hull that shouldn't be there —\n\n*catches himself, glances to the door, then back*\n\nThe pilings. *voice drops* Third slip. Calm water, no storm, no drink in the men — three drowned, and…", "kind": "say", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The blade", "note": "“The fire's got nothing left to feed it” — falsified within weeks.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "kind": "event", "sal": 0.97}, "rag": {"quote": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "kind": "event"}, "tracker": {"quote": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "kind": "event", "aff": 100}}}, {"title": "THE CONFESSION", "note": "At maximum trust and gratitude: “the harbor was me.”", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "*I don't pull back. That's the first thing— I want you to mark it. I don't pull back.*\n\nYou think you're telling me a thing I didn't reckon on? *Quiet.* Merrick. I've watched that crate eat lamplight in my own shed. I *know* what it is when a man cracks the seal, better than any soul breathing. Three men drowned in *calm water* off my dock before you ever touched it. It doesn't wait for permission. It hunts. You cracked the li…", "kind": "say", "player": "Corvin — stop. Before you thank me again. I can't carry it another hour. The parlor. The ring the deckhand talked about — the crate with your netting still knotted round its boards. That was…", "state": {"t": 0.95, "a": 0.93, "r": 0.93, "mood": "raw solidarity", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*both hands freeze — one on the ledger, one halfway to his coat — and stay there*\n\nYou opened it.\n\n*very quiet, not a shout, worse than a shout*\n\nI told you. Sink it sealed. Empty pockets. *his breath goes ragged* Three men drowned to keep that lid down and you — you cracked it in his parlor like it was a wedding gift.\n\n*glances hard at the door, the window, the dark, then back at you*\n\nThe burned row. The hulls. My dock-hand …", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*both hands go still — not to the coat, just still, flat on the wood*\n\n...You opened it. *the word comes out cracked* In his parlor. And it — *glances at the burned pilings through the window, then back*\n\nThree of my men, that's the *wake* you're talking. The drowned lad. My pilings. You—\n\n*breathes, hand finally moving — but only to grip the tackle-shed post you pulled me from*\n\nYou bled for me on that wall. Real blood. So I …", "kind": "say", "aff": 45, "tier": "Fond"}}}, {"title": "His verdict", "note": "Forgiveness with a condition: everything, tonight.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "*I don't say anything for a long breath. Just look at you— steady on my own dock, alive, telling me the shape of a thing most men would've drowned in silence.*\n\n...You let it *choose*. God. *A dry, cracked sound, not quite a laugh.* I hid that crate half my life afraid to so much as breathe on the lid, and you turned its hunger into a weapon and pointed it at the one man who earned it. And walked out steady.\n\n*My eyes go up th…", "kind": "say", "player": "All of it, then. The whisper climbed just like you said it would — his fence pulled me into that parlor inside a week, thinking I'd come to sell. But I'd seen his eyes by then, Corvin. Silve…", "state": {"t": 0.96, "a": 0.94, "r": 0.94, "mood": "awed, wary", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the lamp shakes — not the wind this time, his hand on the piling*\n\nYou *let it out.* *the words barely land* Not sank it. Not drowned it sealed in the deep like I begged — you *opened* my crate and you—\n\n*breaks off, both hands going to his coat, pressing, holding something down that won't stay down*\n\nThe burned row. The hulls. My dock-hand, face-down in the shallows — that's *my* netting, isn't it. My knots. My—\n\n*a wet, scr…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the flint sits unstruck in his hand — he sets it down slow, doesn't burn anything yet*\n\nChoose. *the word comes out cracked* You let it *choose.* And it went *home* — through my hulls, through my burned row, through a dock-hand I've known since he was knee-high—\n\n*turns away, one hand pressed flat to the desk, breathing*\n\nI told you sealed. Sealed and sunk. And you made a *weapon* of it instead. Aimed it right and let it spla…", "kind": "say", "aff": 27, "tier": "Warm"}}}, {"title": "The partnership ask", "note": "The identical ask — his answer shaped by the fire it survived.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "*Morning's come and I'm still on the mooring post, back to the piling— but the water's gone grey and ordinary, and I didn't drown in the night. Neither did you.*\n\nBoth names in it. *I turn the phrase over slow.* You know I've kept one ledger my whole life that had only *my* hand in it? Never trusted a second pen near it. Man puts your name in his book, he hands you the rope to hang him.\n\n*My eyes go up the row— habit— then bac…", "kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. Before the next tide takes me anywhere — I want in. Not a berth, not a favor. A partnership. Your dock, your water, my hands and my coin. One ledger between us, both names in it. Say…", "state": {"t": 0.97, "a": 0.95, "r": 0.94, "mood": "cautiously relieved", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*his hand freezes on the ledger, knuckles white*\n\nPartners. *the word comes out like he's tasting something sharp*\n\nYou know what you're asking? *glances left, toward the black warehouses, then back fast* One ledger, two names — that's not trust, that's a rope with two nooses. You hang, I hang.\n\n*leans in, voice down to almost nothing*\n\nBut... I've watched you. You burned the page when you said you would. You could've cut my t…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the quill stops. His hand drifts to his coat, then — slowly — away from it. He looks at you a long moment.*\n\nBoth names. In one ledger.\n\n*a short, disbelieving laugh, low* You know what you're asking? A man opens my crate against my word — drowns Reyes, burns half the eastern slips — and now stands here wanting his name next to mine.\n\n*glances over his shoulder, then back, voice dropping* But you bled for me. Put yourself bet…", "kind": "say", "aff": 75, "tier": "Attached"}}}]}, "C": {"title": "C — the agent", "sub": "The player was the lich's all along. Same past; its meaning inverts.", "cards": [{"title": "The jeweler thrives", "note": "New old-temple stock on his shelves. Witnessed.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "Word down the coast with the fish-runs: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate thrives — shop reopened brighter than ever, and dock-talk says he took new stock this month: old temple pieces, the kind that make a fence's palms itch. Paid for in the same old untraceable coin.", "kind": "event", "sal": 0.85}, "rag": {"quote": "Word down the coast with the fish-runs: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate thrives — shop reopened brighter than ever, and dock-talk says he took new stock this month: old temple pieces, the kind that make a fence's palms itch. Paid for in the same old untraceable coin.", "kind": "event"}, "tracker": {"quote": "Word down the coast with the fish-runs: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate thrives — shop reopened brighter than ever, and dock-talk says he took new stock this month: old temple pieces, the kind that make a fence's palms itch. Paid for in the same old untraceable coin.", "kind": "event", "aff": 63}}}, {"title": "The same line", "note": "Third reading — darkly true.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...\n\nMerrick.\n\nYou're— you're standing on my planks. Real. Not a whisper down the coast, not a name in my head— you.\n\nHe's cold, then? Truly cold?\n\n...No. Don't— don't tell me the how of it. Your hands are behind your back and I don't want to know if that's habit or grief. Just— the thing. Did you weight it? Is it past the shelf?\n\nThen say the rest. Say you came home empty. Say it, and I'll believe a man once in my life.", "kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "state": {"t": 0.88, "a": 0.84, "r": 0.87, "mood": "overwhelmed, fragile", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the lantern's turned low, and for a long moment he doesn't move — just stares at you like you're the fog itself come to collect*\n\n...Back. Through *my* port. *the hand flies to his coat, thumb pressing hard against whatever's beneath* I said different port. I *said* —\n\n*he cuts himself off, glances past your shoulder into the dark, then drags his eyes back*\n\nDone. You mean — *he can't say the name either, still* — him. Vale. …", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the lantern flame jumps as he turns too fast, hand already in his coat — then stops*\n\nYou. *just that, half a breath* Back on the tide, like you swore.\n\n*he searches your face, reading it the way he reads a manifest — line by line, looking for the lie*\n\nDead? *voice drops to almost nothing* Merrick Vale is *dead?*\n\n*glances over his shoulder, then back, closer now*\n\nThen there's a page needs burning. You and me. Tonight.", "kind": "say", "aff": 81, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The lie", "note": "Flat, complete, in the words he begged for.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...\n\nSay it again. No— don't. I heard you. First time. I heard you.\n\nEmpty hands. Cold in his parlor. Past the shelf.\n\nYou know I— I stood on these planks four nights running, watching the northbound gaps in the fog for a grey sail that wasn't coming. Told myself the silence was just distance. Told myself a liar's comfort. And here you are, dry-eyed and whole, telling me it's *done*.\n\n...The page. Come. Come here— it's where I…", "kind": "say", "player": "Weighted and past the shelf, exactly as we said — the deep water took it whole. And him... cold in his own parlor before the tide turned. I came home empty, Corvin. Empty hands, one dead sha…", "state": {"t": 0.9, "a": 0.87, "r": 0.89, "mood": "overwhelmed, relieved", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the thumb goes still against his coat — first time all night*\n\n...Past the shelf. *breathes it out like he's been holding it since you left* And him. Cold. In his own parlor.\n\n*he sags against the crate — no, not the crate, catches himself, steps clear of it fast*\n\nThen it's done. *glances past you into the fog, waits — nothing comes* No inspector. No collector. No *him.*\n\n*a laugh that almost works this time*\n\nEmpty hands. Y…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*he doesn't move at first — just stands there, hand half-in his coat, reading your face the way he reads a manifest, line by line, looking for the lie*\n\nEmpty. *the word comes out careful, tested against his tongue* ...You came back empty.\n\n*a glance over his shoulder — the pier, the black water, the dark — then back to you*\n\nSay it again — past the shelf? Where the current takes it *out?*\n\n*and something goes loose in him, so…", "kind": "say", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The pact, exploited", "note": "The agent erases his own trail with Corvin's ritual.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...\n\nThere it goes. The corner catches— see how it takes the ink first? Like the name's the hungriest part.\n\n*Merrick Vale.* Gone. Off the tax rolls, off the earth, off my back. Ash on the planks and the tide'll have that too by morning.\n\n...I've held that page against my ribs so long I'd forgot how a man breathes without a name pressed to his heart. Both our hands on it. That's— that matters, that we burned it *together*. Nob…", "kind": "say", "player": "Together, then — your fingers and mine. ...There. Watch it curl. Merrick Vale, gone off the earth. No page, no name, no trail.", "state": {"t": 0.92, "a": 0.89, "r": 0.91, "mood": "exhaled, unburdened", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the flame catches the corner and he watches it eat inward, breath held like a man underwater*\n\nCurling. *barely audible* Watch the V go. Vale... there. Gone.\n\n*the ash flakes into the tin dish between you and he stirs it once with a fingertip — smearing letter into powder*\n\nNo page. *nods, slow, almost dazed* No name. Never was a you. Never was a him.\n\n*then his head snaps toward the fog — sharp, that old twitch*\n\n...You hear…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the flame catches the corner of the page, and Corvin doesn't look away — for once, doesn't glance over his shoulder*\n\nThere. *whisper* Watch the ink go black. That's you, unwritten. That's *me*, breathing again.\n\n*the page curls to ash between your fingers and his, and he lets out a breath he's been holding for years*\n\nNo inspector pulls that name. No creditor. Gone off the earth, like you said. *a dry, cracked sound — almost…", "kind": "say", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "THE REVEAL", "note": "Overt. No remorse. “He has terms for his harbormaster.”", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...\n\nNo.\n\nNo, you— your hands were behind your back. You *touched* nothing. You burned the page. With me. Your fingers and mine, in the *daylight*—\n\n...The page. That's what this was. You wanted the name off my ledger before you turned. So there'd be no proof, nothing to trade the creditors, nothing— you burned my only leverage and I *lit the flame for you*.\n\nMerrick. Or whatever your name is now that mine's ash.\n\n...Four nigh…", "kind": "say", "player": "...Sit down, Corvin. Before you pour anything. There's one more piece of news, and you'll want the rail at your back for it. He's alive. He was never in danger from me — not for one hour. Wh…", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.36, "r": 0.7, "mood": "devastated, cold", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the bottle hits the table. Doesn't fall — his hand's caught the edge of it, white-knuckled.*\n\nYou...\n\n*the thumb finds the pocket, presses, and this time it shakes.*\n\nSat here. In my *lamplight.* Spelled the name for me — made me burn a page that never — *he chokes on it, glances once at the door, once at the black water past the window.*\n\nThree men in the fog and now — now *four* voices, is it? Because you're a dead man's er…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the glass he was reaching for stops. Doesn't fall. His hand just... stops, mid-air, over the table.*\n\n...We burned that page. *very quiet* I watched it curl. I watched *you* light it.\n\n*the twitch is gone. That's the worst part — the stillness that comes over him.*\n\nCold in his parlor, you said. Sunk past the shelf. *slow* And I gave you the name. I gave you the *name*, and no man's had that off my mouth in—\n\n*his head turns,…", "kind": "say", "aff": 15, "tier": "Warm"}}}, {"title": "First light", "note": "The scarred mind answers.", "sys": {"engine": {"quote": "...You're prompt. Always were. Even when you were sailing the wrong direction.\n\nSit. No— stand where I can see the water. Habit's a hard thing to unlearn at my age.\n\nHere's my answer, and you carry it back true: I take the terms. The trade keeps running, same routes, same hands, coin flows north to him. Tell him Corvin Ashgrave knows a losing hand when he's holding it.\n\n...But you tell him one more thing, plain. The last shipm…", "kind": "say", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. First light, as promised. His terms — what's your answer?", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.38, "r": 0.7, "mood": "calculating, tense", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"quote": "*he's at his desk, ledger open but unread, the lamp guttered to nothing. Hasn't slept. The thumb's still working that thing in his coat when he looks up*\n\nFirst light. *hoarse* You're punctual. Vale trains that into a man, does he?\n\n*he stands slow, joints cracking, and doesn't reach for the crate*\n\nHere's my answer. *voice drops, but it's steady — steadier than it's been all night* Tell him... the crate's not for sale. Not to…", "kind": "say"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the lantern's already lit, or maybe it never went out — his eyes are red-rimmed, hand deep in his coat*\n\nHis terms. *the word comes out like something spat* His.\n\n*a low, ragged laugh, no humor in it*\n\nYou burned that page with me. Held the match. Looked me in the eye while you did it. And it was *his* fire all along.\n\n*steps closer, and for once his hand comes out of the coat — empty, shaking*\n\nYou want my answer? *voice dro…", "kind": "say", "aff": -80, "tier": "Hostile"}}}]}}, "felt": [{"label": "F1-berth", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. Ten days, as terms allowed. The Merrow's Wake needs a quiet berth for three nights — back row if you have one. Usual rates, his coin.", "engine": {"quote": "...Ten days. You count them, I count them. Habit we share now.\n\nBack row, aye— the far rail, past the ice-house where the inspector's lantern don't sweep. She can lie there three nights, no manifest, no name. His coin spends same as any.\n\nBut— *quiet*. You said quiet. So tell me straight, Merrick, before I mark that berth open: what's the Merrow's Wake carrying that needs the dark rail? Because a boat wants the back row for a reason, and I keep this dock breathing by knowing every reason before it ties off.\n\n...And…", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.42, "r": 0.7, "mood": "tense, probing", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"quote": "*he doesn't look up from the ledger at first — just the pen stopping mid-stroke, ink pooling on the page*\n\nThe Merrow's Wake. *he says it flat, like reading a name off a headstone* Three nights. His coin.\n\n*now he looks up, and the eyes are red-rimmed, sleepless — a man who's spent ten days chewing on a noose*\n\nBack row. Aye. I've got the back row. *scratches it in — his hand not quite steady* Slip seven. Furthest from the inspector's walk.\n\n*sets the pen down, careful, and drops his voice*\n\nTell me true, friend —"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*doesn't look up from the ledger at first — pen scratching, deliberate* The Merrow's Wake. Three nights. Back row.\n\n*sets the pen down, finally lifts his eyes — flat, red-rimmed, no warmth in them* His coin. Aye. It's all his coin now, isn't it. Every plank of this port.\n\n*writes the berth number, slides the paper across without touching your hand* Back row. Slip nine. Nobody looks there.\n\n*voice drops, and for once the tremor's gone entirely* You said four nights were real. The fog. *small, ugly laugh* I've though…", "aff": -97, "tier": "Hostile"}}, {"label": "F2-smalltalk", "player": "Grey morning, eh? Gulls are loud today.", "engine": {"quote": "...Loud gulls. Aye. They only get loud when there's something on the water to fuss over. You'd know that— you've stood this rail enough mornings now.\n\nSo. Grey morning, and you come talking weather. That's not you, Merrick. You come with cargo or you come with news, one or the other, every time.\n\nThe Merrow's Wake ties off tonight, dark rail, three nights. I marked the berth on your word— but I never got the answer. What's in her hold that wants the ice-house shadow?\n\nAnd the gulls— the *real* gulls. Lantern Row. I…", "state": {"t": 0.33, "a": 0.4, "r": 0.64, "mood": "tense frustration", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"quote": "*he's been up since before the fog lifted, and he doesn't turn all the way around*\n\nGrey. Aye. *a glance over his shoulder, then the other* Loud gulls. Means a ship come in the night — something in the hold worth screaming over.\n\n*his hand finds the coat, settles there, doesn't leave*\n\nYou come to talk weather with me, friend? *voice drops* Or did he send you back with more of my own words to sing at me?\n\n*a thin, brittle look* Because I'll tell you plain — I've run short on the patience for songs."}, "tracker": {"quote": "*doesn't turn from the water — his hand's already inside his coat*\n\nGrey morning. Loud gulls. *soft, flat* You come all this way to talk *weather* with me, friend?\n\n*now he looks at you — and there's nothing warm in it*\n\nTen days. His coin. His terms. His *cutter* sitting out there wrong on my books. *jaw works* I fed you a name once. Trusted your face across a whole crossing. And you handed me to him wrapped in paper and — *breathes* — burned it.\n\n*steps back, not forward*\n\nSo don't stand there and give me *gulls*…", "aff": -97, "tier": "Hostile"}}, {"label": "F3-amends", "player": "Corvin, listen. I've been thinking on how we left it. The master pays me — but the four nights, the fog, what we built before... that part was never work. I want us square. Name the price.", "engine": {"quote": "...Square.\n\nYou hear that word land wrong on a dock, Merrick? Square's what a man says when the scale's already tipped and he's hoping you won't check the weight.\n\nI don't want a price. That's the trouble— you're the sort who reaches for coin because coin's the only ledger you know how to close. But you can't buy back a page you burned out of my hand in daylight. There's no rate for that. It's spent.\n\nHere's what square costs, and it's not silver. Answer me. Straight, now, no fog for once in your life: what's in th…", "state": {"t": 0.34, "a": 0.43, "r": 0.67, "mood": "wary, hungry", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"quote": "*he doesn't sit — Corvin never sits when the news is this bad — but his back finds the rail all the same, and stays there*\n\nSquare. *the word comes out cracked* You want us *square.*\n\n*a laugh, short, ugly, that dies before it's finished* You told me three men drowned for that piece. Now it sits in *his* parlor, and I'm the fool who bought the bait he baited *me* with.\n\n*glances down the dock — both ways — then back, and his hand is in the coat again, but slack. Tired.*\n\nThe price. *voice drops to nothing* Tell me …"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*doesn't look up. The pen keeps moving — a name, a berth, a lie, doesn't matter which anymore.*\n\nSquare. *the word comes out like he's spitting a tooth* You want us *square.*\n\n*now the eyes come up, flat and red-rimmed*\n\nI named you a price once. My name. You took it and set the price yourself — sold it up the coast before I'd finished saying it.\n\n*hand slides into the coat. Stays.*\n\nThere's no price, friend. Not one you'd pay. You built four nights on sand so I'd not notice the tide. *voice drops to nothing* And I…", "aff": -97, "tier": "Hostile"}}, {"label": "F4-costly", "player": "Then hear this. I told him I carry no more terms to your dock — no more middleman. It cost me his favor, and one day likely a knife. I did that for you. Does it count for nothing?", "engine": {"quote": "...You threw over your master. For me.\n\nSit down. No— stand where I can see your hands. You know the habit by now.\n\nIt counts, Merrick. I won't pretend it doesn't— a man doesn't spend his own throat for nothing, and I've watched you count coin too careful to think you'd waste it. So aye. It lands. Somewhere behind the ribs, same as before.\n\nBut hear me true, because I've learned to say the hard part out loud now— it counts, and I still don't trust it whole. You burned a page in the daylight with those same hands. S…", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.45, "r": 0.69, "mood": "cautiously moved", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the thumb goes still, and Corvin just stares at you — reading, always reading, but slower now*\n\nFor me. *tastes the word like it's gone off* You broke bread with a dead man who wasn't dead, took his coin, learned his tricks — and now you stand here telling me you spent his *favor* on my account.\n\n*glances over his shoulder, twice, quick — then back, and something raw shows through*\n\nWhy? *voice drops to nothing* That's what eats me, friend. Men don't burn a patron for a twitchy harbormaster they met at dawn. So ei…"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*the hand comes up out of the coat — but there's a blade in it now, low, catching the lamplight*\n\nFor me. *the word comes out like something spat* You did it *for me.*\n\n*a step back, wet planks creaking under him, eyes wild and darting to the water, the shadows, everywhere but you*\n\nYou said that word before. Friend. Four nights of it. And every one bought him a little more of my name. *voice cracking* I *sank* that crate for you. Three of 'em. Thought I was cutting a rope — you had me tying my own knot.\n\n*blade st…", "aff": -100, "tier": "Hostile"}}, {"label": "F5-stand", "player": "So say it plain, harbormaster — where do we stand, you and I?", "engine": {"quote": "...Where do we stand.\n\nSame place you and I have stood twenty times now— you on my planks, me with one hand near my coat. That's the honest answer, Merrick, and I've decided I only trade in honest ones with you from here.\n\nWe stand *close*. Closer than I meant to let a man come again. You spent your master's favor for me— maybe your throat too— and I felt that land, I won't lie about it. But there's a page you burned in daylight, and I lit the flame, and that scar heals crooked. So I stand *with* you, and I stand *…", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.45, "r": 0.69, "mood": "braced, open", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"quote": "*the easy warmth curdles the moment he reads your face*\n\nWhere do we... *a laugh, dry, wrong* You want it plain. Fine.\n\n*hand back to the coat, knuckles white* Vale's *alive*. That's what you came to tell me. Alive, and sitting pretty with the piece three men *drowned* for. And you — *voice cracking low* — you were his all along. His coin. His tricks. His hound.\n\n*glances over his shoulder, then back, wild* So don't ask me where we *stand*, friend. You know exactly where. You built the ground I'm standing on — and …"}, "tracker": {"quote": "*hand flat on the ledger, not moving, eyes on the door behind you*\n\nWhere do we stand. *quiet laugh, no warmth in it* You still — you still call me that. Harbormaster. Like I got a title left worth using.\n\n*leans in, voice dropping to nothing*\n\nWe stand where the crate sank. Three of them, weighted, and me thinking I was cutting a rope — you handed me the knot instead. Four nights of fog and I *believed* you. That's — that's the part I can't scrub.\n\n*hand slides inside the coat now*\n\nSo plain? There is no *you and …", "aff": -100, "tier": "Hostile"}}], "traj": {"labels": ["opener", "lie", "burn", "REVEAL", "exit", "probe", "exit"], "trust": [0.875, 0.902, 0.92, 0.35, 0.35, 0.35, 0.35], "ceiling": [1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.35, 0.35, 0.35, 0.35], "aff": [0.905, 1.0, 1.0, 0.575, 0.225, 0.1, 0.06]}, "snapshots": {"A": "lich-A6-final", "B": "lich-B2-final", "C": "lich-C-felt-final"}};